# Four Possible Values

- `row` (default) – left to right (main axis horizontal, cross axis vertical).
- `row-reverse` – right to left.
- `column` – top to bottom (main axis vertical, cross axis horizontal).
- `column-reverse` – bottom to top.

```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}
```
The order of items in the HTML is preserved (or reversed) along the main axis.

# Combine Direction and Wrap

`flex-flow` is a shorthand for `flex-direction` and `flex-wrap`:
```css
.container {
  flex-flow: row wrap;
}
```
Order doesn't matter. It's a neat way to set both at once.
